# Single-page app fallback.
#
# Every route below is rendered by React Router in the browser, so there is no
# file on disk at /matches or /majors/computer-science. Without this, a cold
# load of any of them — a bookmark, a shared link, a refresh — is a 404 from
# Cloudflare Pages before the app ever boots. The 200 (rather than a redirect)
# is what keeps the original URL in the address bar for the router to read.
#
# /api is deliberately absent: Phase 7 put the Worker on the same origin, and
# Pages Functions are matched before this file, so API requests never reach it.
# Confirmed against `wrangler pages dev` — /api/health answers from the
# Function while /matches falls through to index.html.
#
# ---- Two things learned in Phase 7, so nobody "fixes" this file ----
#
# 1. `wrangler pages dev` rejects the rule below on every run:
#
#        Found 1 invalid redirect rule:
#        Infinite loop detected in this rule and has been ignored.
#
#    It is a false positive in wrangler's local validator, which reasons that
#    rewriting to /index.html re-matches /* — the platform does not, and this
#    is the pattern Cloudflare's own SPA guidance uses.
#    See https://github.com/cloudflare/workers-sdk/issues/11824.
#
# 2. Deep links work even when the rule is ignored, because Pages' own HTML
#    handling already serves index.html for a path that matches no asset. So
#    this file is redundancy rather than the load-bearing piece it was written
#    as. It stays: the fallback is a platform default, defaults change, and a
#    stated rule costs one line.
#
#    The same default has one edge worth knowing — a request for a missing
#    /assets/*.js chunk also returns index.html with a 200, so a tab left open
#    across a deploy receives HTML where it expects JavaScript. That is the
#    exact failure the Phase 5 error boundary's second state was built for.
/*    /index.html   200
